<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <p role="eyebrow">Analytical lens · System before surface</p>
      <h2>A medium is a system</h2>
      <grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill">
        <grid-item colspan="25" vertical-align="center">
          <p>Tools and formats shape what can be made. Infrastructures shape circulation. Interfaces shape perception, while conventions shape participation.</p>
          <grid direction="vertical" divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug">
            <grid-item padding="9pt 0">
              <p><b>Fixed instance</b> · Print stabilizes a version.</p>
            </grid-item>
            <grid-item padding="9pt 0">
              <p><b>Coded state</b> · Digital systems update and respond.</p>
            </grid-item>
            <grid-item padding="9pt 0">
              <p><b>Generated variation</b> · Computational systems generate and vary.</p>
            </grid-item>
          </grid>
          <p font-size="sm">Transformation occurs when these relationships change—not when a surface merely looks new.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="35" vertical-align="center" align="center">
          <diagram prompt="Four forces converge to form a medium system: Tools and formats determine what can be made; Infrastructure determines how work circulates; Interfaces shape perception; Conventions organize participation. The central result is Medium as a system." template-key="inputs" language="English" width="500pt" height="320pt" align="center"></diagram>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>